## Rule

Files touched means distinct files among primary symbol-bearing search hits with positive relevance, excluding the related section. All returned primary hits count, so the size is not bounded by three targets. The first three symbols alone receive impact probes. One or two target files is small, three to seven medium, and eight or more large. Broad refactor/migration wording moves one bucket upward. Dependency breadth lowers confidence by 0, 0.1 or 0.2 for <=3, 4-11 or >=12 dependencies; it does not enlarge the size. Existing specificity/test confidence rules remain. No thresholds were fitted to these PRs.

Dependencies sum the full caller and co-change counts reported for the probed symbols; overlaps between symbols can occur, so this is risk breadth, not a distinct-file edit forecast. Compared with the old first-three raw hits, probing actual symbols can increase this risk count. Nodes include direct caller files, known tests and co-change files, not arbitrary recursive paths from impact output. The contract records full collected node/edge counts before the 40/80 display caps; upstream clipping, omitted probes and invalid paths mark truncated as well.

